---
// The landing page, as an Astro page rather than a hand-written file.
//
// WHY IT MOVED. It used to be site/index.html, copied to the site root by
// scripts/assemble_site.py and seen by nothing else -- not the Astro build,
// not `astro dev`, not a single check that protects the docs. fabric-emulator
// ran the two-surface version and its assembler records how it ended: a
// hand-written root page and an Astro page under /docs/ drifted until the
// version pill read "unreleased" on a repository with 33 tags. One source now,
// served at BOTH doors from one build output.
//
// THE RULE THAT MAKES ONE FILE CORRECT AT TWO DEPTHS: nothing here may be
// page-relative. This exact file is served at /snowflake-emulator/ AND at
// /snowflake-emulator/docs/, so `href="docs/parity/"` resolves to two
// different places and is wrong at one of them.
//
//   base -- where the DOCS live:    /snowflake-emulator/docs/
//   root -- where the SITE root is: /snowflake-emulator/
const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL;
const root = base.replace(/docs\/$/, "");
---
<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="utf-8">
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
<title>Snowflake Emulator — a Snowflake account on localhost</title>
<meta name="description" content="Official Snowflake connectors and unmodified dbt-snowflake against a local account. SQL runs on DuckDB, and anything the emulator cannot do is refused by name rather than quietly ignored.">
<link rel="icon" href="data:image/svg+xml,<svg xmlns='http://www.w3.org/2000/svg' viewBox='0 0 100 100'><text y='.9em' font-size='90'>❄</text></svg>">
<style>
